/-!
# Parent geometry of the same literal normalized family

Both capacities use the original parent width and preselected gap.
The full sixth-root deletion changes the support allowance, but keeps
that parent width. The original injective occurrence maps control the
slot counts, and the calculated child data preserve kappa and theta.
These are proofs about the actual normalization constructor, before
or after its existing choice of capacity children.
-/

noncomputable section
open scoped Classical BigOperators NumberField nonZeroDivisors SchwartzMap

namespace HeckeSkeleton.Moments.EngineStep

open NumberField IsDedekindDomain DedekindZetaZeroFree LocalFiniteSums
open HeckeGeneral.Arithmetic HeckeGeneral.Characters HeckeGeneral.Analysis
